WEBVTT

00:02.547 --> 00:04.676
<i>Taiyo? Kyoichiro? My bad.</i>

00:04.676 --> 00:07.264
<i>I just finally managed
to break through the defense system.</i>

00:07.264 --> 00:09.937
<i>I'm relaunching the
"Stop the Seed-Sowing Project" mission.</i>

00:11.105 --> 00:12.233
Roger that.

00:13.401 --> 00:16.032
We've arrived at the gate
to the deepest part of the hideout.

00:16.032 --> 00:18.829
It's going to be a race
to see who can stop them first.

00:20.415 --> 00:22.879
Starting now, we're switching gears
to capture Kawashita.

00:22.879 --> 00:24.465
Get ready, Taiyo.

00:24.465 --> 00:25.300
Right.

00:30.060 --> 00:31.271
Whirlwind.

00:31.271 --> 00:32.356
Ascending Waterfall.

00:40.497 --> 00:42.167
Oh, come on.

00:42.167 --> 00:44.840
That door was custom-built, you know.

00:50.058 --> 00:51.603
Hey there, Taiyo Asano.

00:52.187 --> 00:54.735
Thanks for looking after Hakuja
on the train.

00:55.653 --> 00:57.072
Kawashita!

00:57.657 --> 01:01.039
Don't take the bait, Taiyo. It's a trap.

01:01.665 --> 01:05.965
Shion found the link between the
detonation system and his biometric data.

01:06.967 --> 01:09.890
If any damage
is inflicted on his body…

01:10.892 --> 01:13.188
this hideout will blow up.

01:17.739 --> 01:19.951
Oh, man, I'm busted, huh?

01:20.369 --> 01:24.251
As long as the Seed-Sowing Project
works out, I don't care if I die.

01:25.295 --> 01:28.761
And I've set up another deterrent,
just in case.

01:30.013 --> 01:31.015
Nanao!

01:32.101 --> 01:37.027
Which will be the first to fall,
this base or your youngest sibling?

01:37.027 --> 01:38.238
Want to take a guess?

01:57.276 --> 02:06.837
MISSION: YOZAKURA FAMILY

03:14.471 --> 03:17.604
PLAN 25
AI AND MIZUKI

03:17.604 --> 03:18.772
Wh-What on earth?

03:19.481 --> 03:21.862
It's an emergency! Just make a run for it!

03:23.741 --> 03:25.368
What do you think you're doing?

03:25.368 --> 03:27.790
Don't mind me!
You guys need to go on ahead!

03:27.790 --> 03:29.168
R-Right.

03:39.063 --> 03:40.440
What a pity.

03:43.321 --> 03:46.369
Your mission appears to be incomplete.

03:46.870 --> 03:49.333
MIZUKI HAZAKURA EFFICIENCY 488%
(NUMBER 3 IN THE NIJIBANA)

03:51.087 --> 03:52.339
Is this…

03:56.013 --> 03:57.767
sleeping gas?

03:58.059 --> 04:02.777
Correct. I'm going to send this gas
from the air vent through the pipes

04:02.777 --> 04:04.781
and flood the passageway with it.

04:10.751 --> 04:14.216
In a few minutes,
the test subjects who attempted escape

04:14.216 --> 04:16.011
will all have been captured.

04:19.769 --> 04:24.361
Ah, I see that you have
astounding regenerative power.

04:25.113 --> 04:28.829
To think that you'd neutralize my poison,
even when it's in the air,

04:28.829 --> 04:30.624
that's truly impressive.

04:32.252 --> 04:33.881
That said, it's futile.

04:34.298 --> 04:35.676
Your strategy…

04:38.264 --> 04:40.226
will be thwarted by Ms. Ai.

04:43.024 --> 04:45.361
Give my friends back to me, mister!

04:45.905 --> 04:48.409
AI OUTPUT EFFICIENCY 310%
(NUMBER 6 IN THE NIJIBANA)

04:48.702 --> 04:50.121
What are you going to do?

04:50.121 --> 04:52.292
Waste away and die here?

04:53.085 --> 04:53.962
Or else…

04:54.463 --> 04:57.553
Please just stop! This is just senseless!

04:59.223 --> 05:02.522
You must be test subjects yourselves.

05:02.522 --> 05:04.108
You have no reason to fight.

05:06.195 --> 05:09.619
Are you just going to martyr yourselves
for Kawashita here?

05:10.120 --> 05:14.419
My research can help you regain a body
that doesn't rely on Hazakura,

05:14.671 --> 05:17.175
and I'll also help you
reintegrate into society!

05:17.175 --> 05:18.136
So…

05:21.518 --> 05:24.439
We already have a way
to remove the Hazakura.

05:25.233 --> 05:29.241
We wouldn't die if this base exploded,
and most of all…

05:31.872 --> 05:33.457
we have no society to return to.

05:35.838 --> 05:38.510
It may be an example
of little significance,

05:38.510 --> 05:41.223
but my family was murdered by society.

05:42.518 --> 05:45.481
I wonder if you're familiar with it.

05:46.317 --> 05:48.572
The alleged contamination case
in Zenshotencho

05:48.572 --> 05:51.493
and the unnatural deaths of several
company directors 11 years ago?

05:53.039 --> 05:57.965
In the town where we lived, there was
a sudden outbreak of a mysterious ailment.

05:58.592 --> 06:01.388
And people started dying
one after the other, like so many flies.

06:02.098 --> 06:03.894
Our studies showed that the cause

06:04.144 --> 06:08.779
was soil contamination
by a nearby chemical plant.

06:09.739 --> 06:11.660
We took them to court,

06:11.660 --> 06:15.668
but we were suing a major corporation
backed by the government,

06:15.668 --> 06:18.715
so from the start, we never had a chance.

06:22.389 --> 06:24.978
TOP EXECUTIVES FOUND INNOCENT
To make matters worse, the press
and social media slammed us

06:24.978 --> 06:28.442
DARK SIDE OF THE VICTIMS' GROUP
as a special-interest group
playing the victim card to cash in.

06:32.450 --> 06:35.081
Society had rejected us.

06:37.460 --> 06:40.008
In my despair, I had no choice

06:40.008 --> 06:44.141
but to accept my fate
of being infected and doomed to die.

06:44.559 --> 06:46.061
It was then…

06:46.478 --> 06:48.775
that I caught the eye of Dr. Kawashita,

06:48.775 --> 06:52.742
who deemed my deteriorating body
as useful for Hazakura research.

06:53.492 --> 06:56.708
That's right.
He brought me true salvation.

06:57.918 --> 06:59.756
So that's what this is about.

07:00.883 --> 07:04.056
That's the kind of group Tanpopo is.

07:04.557 --> 07:06.185
It's more or less the last refuge

07:06.185 --> 07:09.399
for those who've lost
the place where they belong.

07:09.901 --> 07:11.361
You think you can save us?

07:11.361 --> 07:12.573
Don't be so arrogant!

07:14.326 --> 07:18.084
Let me show you the pain
of being destroyed from within.

07:28.939 --> 07:31.068
Sounds familiar, doesn't it?

07:32.655 --> 07:34.867
The death throes of a family member.

07:35.619 --> 07:38.667
You can either watch your kid brother
breathe his last again,

07:38.667 --> 07:42.423
or else attack me right now
so that we can all die together.

07:42.423 --> 07:44.052
Pick whichever you prefer.

07:51.818 --> 07:54.489
I'm not the only one you're fighting.

08:03.925 --> 08:04.927
Sorry we got here late.

08:04.927 --> 08:05.762
Sorry!

08:06.096 --> 08:08.475
Thanks! You were right on time!

08:08.727 --> 08:10.479
Oh, man, Hinagiku, eh?

08:10.981 --> 08:13.653
Chacha's been defeated,
and our security's screwed.

08:14.530 --> 08:15.991
You're late, Hotokeyama!

08:16.491 --> 08:18.495
Nanao had to suffer some pain.

08:18.997 --> 08:19.999
<i>My bad.</i>

08:20.291 --> 08:22.963
The police, Hinagiku, the Spy Association.

08:23.297 --> 08:25.134
With so many organizations in play,

08:25.134 --> 08:27.598
getting all the paperwork in order
is a hassle.

08:28.600 --> 08:30.102
Come on, come on!

08:30.102 --> 08:32.440
Let's give them a real beatdown, Futaba!

08:34.444 --> 08:36.365
Ms. Rin, be gentle, okay?

08:36.532 --> 08:39.622
What are you talking about?
How gentle is this?

08:40.666 --> 08:41.918
Um…

08:42.836 --> 08:44.422
This is it, Kawashita.

08:46.343 --> 08:49.432
Starting now, you're taking on all of us!

08:52.982 --> 08:57.992
MISSION: YOZAKURA FAMILY

08:59.680 --> 09:03.962
MISSION: YOZAKURA FAMILY

09:04.547 --> 09:06.341
All right, Sui!

09:06.341 --> 09:08.095
Let's get this done and over with.

09:08.597 --> 09:09.431
No…

09:14.274 --> 09:15.484
What the--

09:16.194 --> 09:18.533
Mr. Kawashita may be scary…

09:18.533 --> 09:20.662
and maybe my friends all died…

09:20.662 --> 09:23.125
and I have to do things
that I don't want to!

09:23.334 --> 09:24.252
But…

09:24.252 --> 09:25.379
this is all I have!

09:27.383 --> 09:29.805
This is our home!

09:29.805 --> 09:31.350
Don't take it away!

09:32.936 --> 09:36.276
Did you really think that two adults
are enough to cross swords with Ms. Ai?

09:36.778 --> 09:38.030
An okami dog…

09:39.407 --> 09:44.710
She's had okami DNA implanted into her
with Hazakura's power.

09:44.710 --> 09:45.629
A chimera.

09:46.463 --> 09:49.135
Her transformation abilities
tipped me off right away.

09:49.595 --> 09:51.139
The samples Sui and Oga gave me.

09:52.058 --> 09:53.770
Hakuja's records.

09:54.689 --> 09:57.861
It's all thanks to the data
that everyone brought me.

09:58.655 --> 10:00.408
<i>Nanao, are you all right?</i>

10:00.408 --> 10:01.493
Big Bro Taiyo.

10:02.286 --> 10:03.163
<i>Thanks.</i>

10:03.581 --> 10:05.669
<i>Now I can focus on my Blooming.</i>

10:05.669 --> 10:08.006
<i>I'll end this right away,
so hold on a little longer.</i>

10:08.508 --> 10:10.762
Thanks. But don't overdo it, okay?

10:11.096 --> 10:12.516
Oh, I won't overdo it.

10:13.100 --> 10:17.108
Supporting you and the others who are
always fighting on the front lines…

10:22.911 --> 10:24.164
…is my mission.

10:27.838 --> 10:29.090
<i>What's this?</i>

10:29.675 --> 10:31.971
<i>My poison's being absorbed?</i>

10:33.600 --> 10:35.352
<i>The concentration is dropping as well.</i>

10:36.104 --> 10:37.983
<i>So these objects have purifying effects?</i>

10:39.277 --> 10:40.864
My Blooming is Adaptation.

10:41.364 --> 10:44.663
These are crystallized cells
of someinine and immunity substances.

10:45.414 --> 10:49.632
My body can counteract any poison
or environment it comes into contact with.

10:52.094 --> 10:54.349
I've seen the list of test subjects.

10:55.184 --> 10:57.856
At first glance, they all seem
like legitimate applicants,

10:58.357 --> 11:01.279
but most were actually
maneuvered into it by Kawashita.

11:04.954 --> 11:07.834
By robbing them of an environment
they could have adapted to,

11:07.834 --> 11:09.337
he made them dependent on him.

11:10.130 --> 11:12.009
What is that but control?

11:13.345 --> 11:15.767
Everyone has the ability to adapt.

11:16.894 --> 11:18.857
It's not something someone gives you.

11:20.694 --> 11:24.075
It's a power that takes shape
when others have your back.

11:26.162 --> 11:29.753
This is a twisted place
that robs you of that power…

11:30.755 --> 11:32.551
a place that shouldn't exist.

11:35.139 --> 11:36.099
Purifying Sublimation!

11:39.063 --> 11:40.734
<i>Such incredible detoxifying power.</i>

11:41.234 --> 11:42.946
<i>I can't produce my toxins fast enough!</i>

11:43.615 --> 11:44.449
<i>So this is…</i>

11:44.909 --> 11:46.369
<i>the Yozakura blood!</i>

11:53.425 --> 11:55.012
<i>Since I've absorbed the gas,</i>

11:55.012 --> 11:57.726
<i>the test subjects on the other side
of the door are safe, too.</i>

11:58.561 --> 11:59.605
Dr. Nanao!

12:00.481 --> 12:01.399
It's Ms. Ai!

12:03.445 --> 12:05.491
She collapsed all of a sudden
while fighting us!

12:07.663 --> 12:10.167
Her pupils are dilated from Blooming!

12:10.167 --> 12:12.046
And the light they're emitting
is unstable.

12:12.798 --> 12:13.966
This is…

12:13.966 --> 12:16.012
I saw a lot of people like this
back in the day.

12:16.388 --> 12:19.895
When they can't withstand Hazakura's
hyperactive shock, they die.

12:20.897 --> 12:22.651
She'll be gone in a few minutes, if that.

12:23.235 --> 12:24.613
I won't let that happen!

12:29.748 --> 12:33.756
<i>Someinine. In other words, I'll neutralize
the Hazakura with my blood!</i>

12:34.591 --> 12:36.469
<i>If I can just nullify Hazakura's toxicity…</i>

12:38.683 --> 12:39.518
<i>It's not working!</i>

12:40.018 --> 12:43.066
<i>The someinine won't take hold,
and her heart rate's still faint.</i>

12:43.568 --> 12:45.029
<i>At this rate, she'll…</i>

12:45.362 --> 12:46.866
That won't do anything.

12:50.456 --> 12:52.460
The ratio of Hazakura is too small…

12:52.961 --> 12:55.132
so the someinine
is physically overpowering her.

12:56.468 --> 13:00.017
If I pump all of my Para-someinine
into her…

13:02.522 --> 13:04.066
it will balance it out…

13:04.066 --> 13:05.402
and I can save this child.

13:13.418 --> 13:14.713
Hold on a second, please.

13:14.713 --> 13:18.261
Your bodies are completely reliant
on Hazakura.

13:18.261 --> 13:20.349
If you pump it all into her, then you'll…

13:21.602 --> 13:23.063
She looked like her, you see.

13:24.232 --> 13:25.693
Like my dead daughter.

13:26.737 --> 13:29.952
That's why I gave in to temptation.

13:31.412 --> 13:32.666
Oh, come on.

13:32.666 --> 13:35.295
You didn't have to kill her, you know.

13:35.295 --> 13:37.509
She was making a racket,
so I couldn't help myself.

13:37.509 --> 13:39.638
You must've really found it unforgivable.

13:40.890 --> 13:42.476
The child abuse.

13:43.270 --> 13:46.192
Did you see your own daughter in her?

13:48.113 --> 13:51.704
Let's get on with retrieving
the compatible candidates and head back.

13:54.292 --> 13:55.962
And see, it was this huge!

13:55.962 --> 13:59.427
After six months, she seems
to have blended in with the others.

14:00.053 --> 14:02.266
She's turned into a lively little pest.

14:02.266 --> 14:04.103
Hey! Mr. Mizuki!

14:04.103 --> 14:05.397
And Mr. Kawashita, too!

14:07.359 --> 14:10.198
So I'm an afterthought?

14:11.200 --> 14:15.334
How does it feel to be waving to the kid
whose mother's face you melted off?

14:15.960 --> 14:18.048
You're one to talk.

14:18.591 --> 14:21.805
You're going to dispose of that boy
by her side next week, aren't you?

14:21.805 --> 14:25.855
Uh, yeah. His compatibility rate's low,
so I have no more use for him.

14:26.356 --> 14:30.155
Ai's coming along nicely, so I think
I'll keep her around a little longer.

14:33.495 --> 14:35.457
Ms. Ai will end up crying again,
won't she?

14:37.169 --> 14:40.175
Kawashita would kill anyone on a whim,
no matter who it was.

14:41.052 --> 14:46.939
Even though it was to protect Ai from him,
I did frighten her immensely.

14:51.406 --> 14:53.828
Knowing that nothing
traumatized this child

14:53.828 --> 14:56.124
more than being grabbed by the head…

14:58.253 --> 15:01.677
I'm the one who ended up
dragging her into the shadows.

15:05.601 --> 15:08.106
Please return her to the light now.

15:10.235 --> 15:11.320
Right.

15:17.166 --> 15:19.462
Mr. Mizuki… no.

15:22.594 --> 15:24.263
This is goodbye, Ms. Ai.

15:24.765 --> 15:27.352
I apologize for frightening you earlier.

15:27.562 --> 15:30.777
Mr. Mizuki. Your hand, Mr. Mizuki…

15:31.486 --> 15:34.200
it doesn't scare me at all, okay?

15:34.200 --> 15:36.580
So please… please…

15:37.498 --> 15:38.834
Mr. Mizuki!

16:05.930 --> 16:08.853
Big Bro Taiyo, we're all safe over here.

16:09.353 --> 16:12.359
I'm going to resume
liberating the test subjects.

16:12.819 --> 16:14.781
You be careful over there, too, okay?

16:16.201 --> 16:17.662
Thanks, Nanao.

16:18.664 --> 16:20.710
Oh, jeez, that damned Mizuki.

16:21.628 --> 16:24.885
Dying for the sake
of a single person, huh?

16:25.385 --> 16:26.597
What an idiot.

16:30.353 --> 16:31.773
Sorry to keep you waiting, Taiyo.

16:32.316 --> 16:33.484
I've severed the link

16:33.484 --> 16:35.740
between the detonation system
and Kawashita himself.

16:36.073 --> 16:37.702
You can go ahead and attack him now.

16:38.119 --> 16:40.040
Thanks, Big Sis Shion!

16:42.419 --> 16:45.342
"FIRST YAE"
"CLEAR SKIES - UPGRADED"

16:47.555 --> 16:48.974
"THUNDERCLAP"

16:49.266 --> 16:54.109
Today's the last day you'll ever
laugh at someone's life, Kawashita!

17:03.796 --> 17:06.217
You're telling me
not to laugh at another's life?

17:06.969 --> 17:09.390
Every life is inconsequential.

17:09.390 --> 17:11.561
What can you do but laugh?

17:25.380 --> 17:27.510
Stay on alert, Taiyo.

17:32.937 --> 17:35.483
His real name is Makoto Kawashita.

17:35.735 --> 17:40.870
Born on July 28, 1914,
here on Skeleton Island.

17:41.788 --> 17:44.126
1914?

17:44.126 --> 17:47.007
I've been having Shion track his career.

17:47.299 --> 17:50.723
At first, we thought we had him
mixed up with someone else, but…

17:50.723 --> 17:54.313
photos, handwriting,
dissertations, travel records,

17:54.313 --> 17:58.112
info we knew to be rock solid
could be traced back to before the war.

17:59.073 --> 18:01.369
I know it seems incredible,
but that's a fact.

18:02.329 --> 18:05.836
Former army surgeon and
Director of the Kawashita Clinic.

18:06.713 --> 18:10.930
A monster who's been lurking in the
shadows of history for the last 100 years.

18:10.930 --> 18:13.727
Ouch. That's harsh.

18:13.727 --> 18:15.815
I'm just a regular human being.

18:16.023 --> 18:19.781
Who are you people
to tell me that I'm a monster…

18:20.658 --> 18:21.993
Yozakura?

18:23.371 --> 18:26.085
<i>That's not the Hazakura Blooming pattern!</i>

18:26.460 --> 18:28.882
<i>It's the same as our Yozakura…</i>

18:30.051 --> 18:34.936
The field of research on you Yozakuras
has existed for quite some time.

18:37.441 --> 18:42.033
It was right after World War Two started
that I learned about your family.

18:43.119 --> 18:45.457
I graduated at the top of my class
in medical school,

18:45.457 --> 18:48.045
and the top brass
came to me with a secret order.

18:48.547 --> 18:52.805
My mission was to research the lineage of
a family of superhumans called Yozakura

18:52.805 --> 18:56.605
and to work toward sending them
into combat as bioweapons.

18:57.230 --> 18:59.652
I couldn't believe such a family existed,

18:59.652 --> 19:04.077
but the indisputable data and numbers
gave me no room to question it.

19:04.579 --> 19:08.085
I was just one step away
from realizing this goal,

19:08.461 --> 19:13.179
only to have all of my research
covered up when we lost the war.

19:15.559 --> 19:17.062
That doesn't add up.

19:19.107 --> 19:22.239
True, the Yozakuras
once worked directly for the government,

19:22.239 --> 19:25.078
but we became independent in 1895.

19:25.411 --> 19:28.877
There's no record of us working with
the military during World War Two.

19:28.877 --> 19:31.298
There's no way
that you could have done research on us.

19:31.675 --> 19:33.219
You're right. At the time,

19:33.219 --> 19:36.810
the Yozakura family did spurn
the government's requests.

19:37.310 --> 19:40.149
But that didn't hamper
my research whatsoever.

19:43.991 --> 19:45.285
But never mind.

19:46.161 --> 19:48.667
That was a trying era
in all sorts of ways.

19:49.293 --> 19:52.132
The battlefield is never level.

19:52.424 --> 19:56.473
It's the weak who get trampled upon
in the most one-sided way.

19:56.891 --> 19:59.313
Military power, economic power,
political power…

19:59.856 --> 20:02.987
every disparity generates tragedy.

20:05.366 --> 20:07.538
But the Yozakuras' power…

20:08.080 --> 20:12.506
the power of Hazakura
bestows power equally.

20:13.508 --> 20:16.180
I realized something upon learning
about the Yozakura family…

20:16.640 --> 20:20.396
that this power was capable
of creating equality and peace.

20:21.357 --> 20:26.200
It would be a waste to let one family
have a monopoly on such an amazing power.

20:26.910 --> 20:29.707
I'll be happy to put it to everyone's use.

20:32.672 --> 20:33.632
What?

20:38.099 --> 20:40.646
My Blooming is Regeneration.

20:41.146 --> 20:45.823
I can store the DNA of my test subjects,
then regenerate them as backups.

20:46.323 --> 20:49.872
My cherished test subjects
are always supporting me.

20:50.666 --> 20:52.586
Now that you've taken Chacha out,

20:52.586 --> 20:56.010
it's just a matter of time before you
shut down the detonation system.

20:56.260 --> 20:58.640
So I'm going to go activate it manually.

21:03.190 --> 21:04.067
Come back here!

21:08.034 --> 21:08.910
Box Blow!

21:10.831 --> 21:11.833
Calm Storm!

21:15.131 --> 21:16.133
It's not working!

21:16.634 --> 21:19.431
Who knew Hazakura
had that kind of regenerative power?

21:20.308 --> 21:24.567
He had the flower eyes
of a pure-blooded Yozakura's Blooming.

21:25.318 --> 21:27.907
No matter how many years
he spent studying us,

21:28.199 --> 21:31.915
there's no way that he'd be able
to artificially replicate them.

21:34.127 --> 21:36.841
I'll just ask him
about these enigmatic matters directly.

21:37.342 --> 21:40.181
But first, we're going to take care
of what's in front of us.

21:40.181 --> 21:41.016
Right!

21:43.437 --> 21:44.899
"PUPPET CHILD"

21:56.004 --> 21:59.177
I'll pool the Hazakura density
in the areas of attack

21:59.177 --> 22:03.018
and create a point
where his defense will weaken.

22:03.018 --> 22:05.439
There, I'll fire a "Hardened" bullet,

22:05.439 --> 22:07.277
in other words, you yourself, Taiyo.

22:11.118 --> 22:12.580
"PATH OF LIGHTNING"

22:13.038 --> 22:15.167
I'll catch up after I've cleared this up.

22:15.167 --> 22:18.257
You go on ahead
and settle your grudge against him.

22:18.842 --> 22:19.760
Roger that!

23:52.696 --> 23:55.952
OLD BLOOD
